      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "In the title compound, C13H10FN3O2, the mol-ecule has an E conformation with respect to the C=N bond of the hydrazone bridge. The dihedral angle between the isonicotinoyl and fluoro-phenol moieties is 4.03\u2005(4)°, and an intra-molecular O-H⋯N hydrogen bond generates an S(6) ring motif. In the crystal, mol-ecules are linked by N-H⋯N and C-H⋯N hydrogen bonds, forming chains propagating along the a-axis direction. The chains are linked by C-H⋯O hydrogen bonds, resulting in the formation of layers lying parallel to the ab plane. The crystal structure also features π-π inter-actions [centroid-to-centroid distance = 3.6887\u2005(8)\u2005Å]."},
